      "problem": "$$\n\nCalculate $\\int -\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{5}(1-{x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x$ for $|x|>1.$",
      "worked_solution": "$$\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cotangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int -\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{5}(1-{x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{5}}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
